  80.9s | {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ceiz9M4R1En98jDTnCS5R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't deliver the question — the `spike` MCP server's `ask_user` tool timed out after 30s of silence, twice in a row:\n\n```\nMCP server \"spike\" tool \"ask_user\" sent no response or progress for 30s; aborting.\n```\n\nThat's the only mechanism I'm permitted to use to ask you anything, so I've stopped here rather than posing the question some other way. Nothing else has been done on the caching layer.\n\nTwo ways to unblock it:\n- Add a per-server `\"timeout\"` (ms) for `spike` in your MCP settings, or\n- Set `CLAUDE_CODE_MCP_TOOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT` (ms) globally — `0` disables the idle timeout entirely, which is likely what you want for a tool that blocks on human input.\n\nThe second one is probably the right fix, since `ask_user` waits on you by design and will always exceed a 30s idle window. Tell me when it's adjusted and I'll retry the question."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":627,"cache_read_input_tokens":18452,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":627},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"480066c6-7beb-4517-8076-5e0307c2ebe6","uuid":"4ad0a493-fc98-40fe-b5b1-76b4552d01cb","timestamp":"2026-09-04T19:54:48.623Z","request_id":"req_011Ceiz9LH3A9hT2FLUPat5p"}
